        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "Mexico City to Querétaro and San Miguel de Allende"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:5a4836cca1208c95",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "994afc33ebeeae65ac974700310b1dfa6bb832686010d831f1c4622a4fbe4a70",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-translator-20261110-da7adf1e0510432f",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "Your guide meets you in the morning for the drive to Querétaro.\n\nThe city tour takes you through the historic centre. One of the main landmarks is the aqueduct, built in the early 1700s and running across the city. The tour also includes the Casa de la Corregidora and the Church of Santa Rosa de Viterbo, whose architecture combines elements of Mexican Baroque and Islamic tradition.\n\nAfter the tour, we continue to San Miguel de Allende. The city is known for its cobbled streets, pink-stone houses and lively arts scene.\n\nIn the centre stands the Parroquia de San Miguel Arcángel, with its distinctive Gothic façade. On your walk, you can make your way to the Plaza Mayor, where you’ll find restaurants, street performers and live music. Craft shops and galleries sell work by local artists and handmade items.\n\nOvernight in San Miguel de Allende."
    },
